From ddf089a18c7bf9b813b45ff8a273c1ffb9df322e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shibco <cade@parare.al>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gui: accept any buffer size in the driver's range

The driver takes any buffer size in [PIPEASIO_MIN_BUFFER_SIZE,
PIPEASIO_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE], power of two or not, but the panel's own
parseIni still carried the pow2 gate: opening and saving the panel
replaced a working buffer_size = 883 with the 1024 default. The size
combo made it worse by showing any unlisted value as 16 (index-0
fallback), a size below the driver's own floor, and Apply then wrote
that 16 back.

Parse with the range check only, mirroring src/config.c. Drop 16 from
the presets and make the combo editable (int validator across the
driver's range) so an arbitrary stored or typed size is shown and
saved verbatim; the latency readout follows the text, not the index.
Apply rejects unfinished or out-of-range typed text instead of silently
rewriting the last valid value to 1024. Covered in test_panel: parse
bounds, an 883 open -> Apply round trip, typed sizes, and invalid text.

Keep capture-only and playback-only configurations valid, but reject the
zero-input plus zero-output combination before saving. Apply now surfaces
configuration write failures both inline and in a nonblocking critical dialog,
and tells the user whether a successful change was reloaded live or needs a
driver/host restart. GUI tests cover both one-direction modes, zero/zero and
invalid-buffer rejection without a write, save failure, and restart feedback.
